{
  "_readme": "Fixture for codeSyntax.WEB names that differ only by a double versus a single dash. Every name uses the --group--leaf form: color/ink-900 is a primitive carrying a role name, --color--text-primary (group color, leaf text-primary), and the semantic color/text/primary carries --color-text--primary (group color-text, leaf primary). Both are valid CSS custom properties and distinct strings; after dash collapse both read --color-text-primary, which is what a tool that normalizes names on import would store. color/bg/surface and color/bg/card share the bare name --color-bg--surface (the second spelled var(--color-bg--surface)): the existing duplicate error, which the collision check must not report a second time. Scopes, modes, pages and the text-style binding are complete and every text-on-bg pair passes contrast, so the only findings are the two under test.",
